==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-add up.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|of a numerical amount}} To take the [[sum]] of; to [[total]].
#: {{syn|en|sum up|tally|see also [[Thesaurus:summate]]}}
#: {{usex|en|'''Add up''' the prices and find out how much it will cost.}}
#: {{ux|en|When they '''added up''' the vaccine doses from all known and anticipate sources, they didn't have enough.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[accumulate]]; to [[amount]] to.
#: {{syn|en|accrue|mount up|see also [[Thesaurus:accumulate]]}}
#: {{usex|en|If you can save even a couple of dollars per day, it will '''add up''' to a lot over a year.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Christopher Walker|title=The First 49|passage=The bus wound its way up into San Marino, passing through the various small castellos that '''add up''' to form the diminutive country, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To [[make sense]]; to be [[reasonable]] or [[consistent]].
#: {{syn|en|compute|hang together|check out|make sense|track|figure}}
#: {{usex|en|His story just doesn't '''add up'''. Why would he have been at the restaurant the day before the event?}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|date=March 16, 2007|developer=w:Capcom Production Studio 4|location=Europe|level=Turnabout Big Top|scene=Part 3: Investigation, Circus Entrance|publisher=w:Capcom|title=w:Phoenix Wright: Ace Attorney – Justice for All|system=w:Nintendo DS|oclc=911403231|text={{smallcaps|Phoenix}}: (Hmm... Something just isn't '''adding up''' here. I wonder, who they really saw?)}}

